A priority queue is an abstract data type where elements are processed by priority rather than arrival order. A binary heap is a complete binary tree data structure that implements a priority queue efficiently in \(O(\log n)\) time.

Priority Queue Concepts

• Definition: A collection where each item has a priority value. Higher-priority elements exit the queue before lower-priority elements.
• Standard vs. Priority Queue: A normal queue follows First-In, First-Out (FIFO). A priority queue lets important items "cut the line".
• Core Operations:
	• insert(item, priority): Adds a new element.
	• pop() / remove(): Deletes and returns the highest-priority element.
	• peek() / top(): Views the highest-priority element without removing it.

Heap Concepts

• Definition: A specialized tree-based data structure used to back priority queues.
• Shape Property: A complete binary tree where every level is full except possibly the last, which fills from left to right.
• Heap-Order Property:
	• Max-Heap: The parent node is always greater than or equal to its children (root holds the maximum value).
	• Min-Heap: The parent node is always less than or equal to its children (root holds the minimum value).
• Array Storage: Heaps use a contiguous array instead of pointer nodes. For a node at index i:
	• Left child is at 2 * i + 1 (or 2 * i if 1-indexed).
	• Right child is at 2 * i + 2 (or 2 * i + 1 if 1-indexed).
	• Parent is at floor((i - 1) / 2).

Heap Maintenance Operations

• Insert (Swim / Heapify-Up): Place the new element at the end of the array, then swap it upward with its parent until the heap rule is fixed [\(O(\log n)\)].
• Delete Root (Sink / Heapify-Down): Replace the root with the last element in the array, then swap it downward with the proper child until the heap rule is fixed [\(O(\log n)\)].

Common Use Cases

• Dijkstra's Shortest Path Algorithm: Quickly fetch the next closest node.
• Prim's Minimum Spanning Tree: Track the minimum weight edge to expand a graph.
• Huffman Coding: Build optimal prefix trees for data compression.
• Heap Sort: Sort an array in \(O(n \log n)\) time using heap structures.